1
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:05,000
It's open. Come in.

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,580
Rohan-sensei?

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:08,780
Where are you?

4
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:10,520
Over here, Koichi.

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,500
Rohan-sensei!

6
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:15,017
Why are you in the corner?

7
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:18,157
When you asked me over here, you
didn't say you were in panic mode!

8
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:19,957
Please, Koichi, I need your help.

9
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:23,080
I'm in the grasp of an
enemy's stand. What?

10
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:26,240
A stand's in here? Where
is it? What's it do?

11
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:27,900
It's over here.

12
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:29,697
Damn thing adhered itself to my back.

13
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:30,940
It did what?

14
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:37,417
So you're saying there's a
stand attached to your back?

15
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,330
That's right.

16
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,127
It's a very serious dilemma.

17
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:42,007
And I don't know what to do.

18
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:44,037
Can I see what we're dealing with?

19
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:44,950
No way.

20
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,157
But if you don't show it to
me, how am I supposed to...

21
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:51,117
If I expose my back, it'll
kill me and take hold of you.

22
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:54,160
Now burn the pages. Yes. Hear that?

23
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:56,928
Even as we speak, it's
whispering in my ear.

24
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,692
You're not making sense!

25
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:03,317
Wait, this is all some big
joke at my expense, isn't it?

26
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,457
How could you say that?

27
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:07,297
I just told you if I expose
my back, I'm done for!

28
00:01:07,380 --> 00:01:11,917
Oh, I heard you, but how do I know you're
not pulling my leg like you always do?

29
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:12,830
Ugh...

30
00:01:12,913 --> 00:01:14,157
Hit the nail on the head, didn't I?

31
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,077
No, I'm being completely serious!

32
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:17,657
There's a dead body upstairs!

33
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:18,570
What?!

34
00:01:18,653 --> 00:01:19,483
A real dead body?!

35
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,030
So, uh...

36
00:01:22,113 --> 00:01:23,941
What are you doing, Rohan-sensei?

37
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:26,677
Don't worry about that,
just bow on past me.

38
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:28,597
Please, Koichi, you have to see the body.

39
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:29,720
Get going!

40
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,294
Can you tell me what all this is about?

41
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:33,530
Told you.

42
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,934
I'm telling the truth.

43
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:37,430
It's gone.

44
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:39,189
How did it just disappear?

45
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:40,891
Look, Koichi, he's there.

46
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:46,980
You see? It's the man.

47
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:48,840
This is Masazo Kinoto.

48
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,877
After he died, he turned
into a lifeless husk.

49
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:54,197
Wow, that's some really impressive work.

50
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,110
Nice job.

51
00:01:56,060 --> 00:01:58,597
But this isn't the time
to be messing around.

52
00:01:58,680 --> 00:01:59,857
I know you know that.

53
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:00,997
While I'm with you,

54
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:04,737
those stand users the old man and the
photo made are trying to hunt us down.

55
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,177
The only reason I rushed
all the way over here was

56
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:09,157
because I was worried
something happened to you.

57
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,100
Why won't you?

58
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,320
Wait, the stand.

59
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:14,300
Anyway, just be careful.

60
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:16,170
Bye.

61
00:02:16,253 --> 00:02:17,726
Hold on, Koichi, don't leave!

62
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:20,017
I asked you to come here
because I knew those pieces of

63
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,477
shit Josuke and Okuyasu would
just laugh at my predicament!

64
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:26,377
You have to trust me, I
thought we were friends!

65
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:27,900
Keicho!

66
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:32,160
Cheer up, bucko, yes.

67
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:35,189
Disappointment's just
another part of life.

68
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,260
This is infuriating.

69
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,960
I've never been so thoroughly humiliated.

70
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:43,240
Bastard, you're going to pay dearly.

71
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:57,290
Let's go.

72
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:29,860
It's the light of the sun,

73
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:35,320
and it's the light of the light.

74
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:41,600
Let the voice of love take you higher.

75
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:47,127
It's the power of the stars.

76
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:49,597
It's the light

77
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:55,760
of the light.

78
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:12,700
My nails are going through their
signature growth spurt again,

79
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,720
and it's no wonder why.

80
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:21,737
The way your hands run through that
perfectly coiffed hair is just...

81
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:23,380
Consider yourself lucky.

82
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,560
You've nearly escaped death.

83
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:29,820
At least until I fully
transitioned to Kosaku Kawajiri.

84
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:31,660
My old man's such a pest.

85
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:34,657
I can't leave the house without
the Cursed Kodger following me.

86
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:36,597
I even caught him spying on me once.

87
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:39,157
Maybe he thinks you're
out partying too much.

88
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:41,177
And whose fault would it be if I was?

89
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:42,697
I was so pissed at him,

90
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:46,477
I decided to freak him out by shoplifting
right in front of his saggy face.

91
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:50,037
Then I made a beeline to your
place, which I'm sure set him off.

92
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,300
You're insane, girl.

93
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,917
The cops are probably after you right now.

94
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:54,830
Ugh.

95
00:04:54,913 --> 00:04:55,743
Hey, you.

96
00:04:55,826 --> 00:04:57,857
What's the big idea
touching people's bags?

97
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:58,770
What's wrong?

98
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,101
Forget it, baby.

99
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,437
It's not worth our time.

100
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:02,350
The hell?

101
00:05:02,433 --> 00:05:03,263
You a pervert?

102
00:05:03,346 --> 00:05:04,880
Or just a damn pickpocket?

103
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,440
Mariah! Mariah!

104
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:12,580
Oh, shit, babe.

105
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,417
Look, we're already in Mariah.

106
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:15,559
Come on, let's go.

107
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,220
Ow! That freaking hurt!

108
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:21,597
What the hell is your deal?

109
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:24,033
Watch it where you're walking, jerk-off.

110
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,306
You see what he was carrying?

111
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:29,540
It was a bowling pin nail clipper.

112
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:32,297
What kind of breed carries
around something like that?

113
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:33,460
Can you say lame?

114
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,806
You've got the pictures, yes?

115
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,897
Where do you think you're going with them?

116
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:51,920
To the Mariah Grand Hotel.

117
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:53,375
I've no other choice.

118
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,980
You're going to Jotaro?

119
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:56,986
He won't be able to help you.

120
00:05:57,200 --> 00:06:00,494
Your best bet is to call it
quits and burn the pictures.

121
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:05,690
Impressive!

122
00:06:05,773 --> 00:06:08,477
And all while someone could have
been watching from a window.

123
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,940
That was very risky.

124
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,200
There, you see?

125
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:16,969
At some point, almost every
street comes to an intersection.

126
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:18,290
See?

127
00:06:18,373 --> 00:06:21,137
Someone will take a peek at your
back, so crossing's impossible!

128
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:24,897
And since the road is about to
get wider, that means more people!

129
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:27,200
Let's stop all this and go back, yes?

130
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:30,286
You're never going to
make it across the road!

131
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,317
You really think so?

132
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,877
Masazo Kinoto made it
to my house, didn't he?

133
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:37,657
He'd have had to have crossed
an intersection to do so.

134
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:39,622
I'm sure I can pull it off, too.

135
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:41,840
I just need to know how he did it.

136
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:45,040
Aha! Like this!

137
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:50,679
This certainly isn't my most shining
moment, but it'll get me across.

138
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:53,420
Not bad, Rohan Kishibe.

139
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:56,037
But there's something you
haven't thought about.

140
00:06:56,120 --> 00:07:00,826
When Masazo Kinoto was crossing the street,
I stayed as quiet as a church mouse!

141
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:02,580
Hey, dumb shit!

142
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:04,937
Why are you farting along like some slug?

143
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,314
What did you just say?

144
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:07,850
See?

145
00:07:07,933 --> 00:07:09,889
Yo, why don't you turn
around and find out?

146
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:11,200
You're pushing it.

147
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:14,417
The only one who's missing
something here, Cheap Trap, is you.

148
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:16,660
I have something Masazo didn't.

149
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,880
My stand, heaven's door!

150
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,840
What the?! Perfect.

151
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:26,258
Now that that's settled, I
can get to the other side.

152
00:07:27,460 --> 00:07:30,280
I suggest you prepare yourself. Say what?

153
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:31,697
What's going on here?

154
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:33,317
Trust me, you'll never make it!

155
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:36,757
When this is over, you'll be a
shriveled up limp dick of a corpse!

156
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:40,397
You sure talk a good game, but
that's all you're good at, isn't it?

157
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,480
You won't be saying anything soon.

158
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:47,559
WHO THE HELL DO YOU THINK
YOU'RE TALKING TO, BITCH?!

159
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:48,840
What? Huh?

160
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:56,729
It seems there won't be any
major intersections for a while.

161
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:05,880
Hey, do you know if your heaven's door
works on animals? Huh? Huh? Do ya?

162
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:09,920
Yes, it works on any intelligent
animal. Well, in that case,

163
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:13,777
if an animal sees your back, it stands to
reason I'll be able to transfer to them!

164
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:16,020
Much easier than people, yes?

165
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:23,332
That's right, I'll have to be
just as careful around them.

166
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:25,107
God, I hate these creatures.

167
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,040
Their glare is infuriating.

168
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,960
Oh, right cat, beat it!

169
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:33,397
How in the...

170
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:34,580
they're swarming!

171
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:38,918
All it takes is a quick glance from
any one of these little guys, yes?

172
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:42,657
You were right when you said the only
thing I'm good at is talking, yes.

173
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:45,975
But humans aren't the only
living things I can talk to!

174
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:47,530
Bingo!

175
00:08:47,613 --> 00:08:49,077
I summoned those animals here!

176
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:51,100
And they are not happy givers!

177
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:54,557
I just finished telling them that
you love killing cats and dogs!

178
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,228
So imagine what they think!

179
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,200
Sick 'em, buds!

180
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:03,980
Heaven's door!

181
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:07,620
It's no use!

182
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,348
There are too many of them!

183
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:10,677
Yes, I win!

184
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,040
Three, freeze!

185
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:17,174
These animals didn't do anything wrong.

186
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:20,640
Time to get lost, all of you. Shoo!

187
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,760
That sound belongs to...

188
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:25,400
Keicho! What?

189
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:28,617
I thought you were fooling me like always?

190
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:30,337
but I had this nagging feeling,

191
00:09:30,420 --> 00:09:33,497
so I went back to your house and
found you acting just as weird.

192
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:36,657
Even when you got outside, you were
still skulking around the sidewalk?

193
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:38,277
with your back against the wall.

194
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,757
Then there's how you crossed the road.

195
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:43,357
You were telling the truth about
the stand stuck to your back.

196
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,260
This is why I admire you.

197
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,300
You're the real deal, Koichi.

198
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:51,380
A true blue friend to the
very end. It's on your back.

199
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:55,794
So all we have to do is remove that
parasite and we're good to go, right?

200
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:01,090
Reverb!

201
00:10:01,173 --> 00:10:03,260
Special Ability 3! Freeze!

202
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:07,020
Miss Force!

203
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,800
You did it!

204
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:16,800
It's not that easy.

205
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,637
I'm clinging to you with my special
ability and not brute strength.

206
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:25,485
If you try to rip me off, you'll just end
up destroying your back in the process.

207
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,220
Now tell Koichi, yes?

208
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:30,940
Come on, you better hurry and spit it out.

209
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,300
What, Rohan-sensei?

210
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,247
I'm grateful to you, Koichi.

211
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:38,151
The fact that you would help
me has truly touched my heart.

212
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:42,420
but I'd appreciate it if
you'd withdraw act three.

213
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:44,820
You can't see it from there,

214
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:48,353
but it would seem my back is
starting to rip itself open.

215
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:53,140
Act three, withdraw three
frees on the double.

216
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,600
S-H-I-T, withdraw completed.

217
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:58,840
Hey, you okay, Rohan sensei?

218
00:10:58,980 --> 00:10:59,960
How bad is it?

219
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:02,238
How bad does it look, Koichi Hirose?

220
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:05,320
You're the reason he's in this mess.

221
00:11:06,140 --> 00:11:09,500
Understand now, Rohan,
you can't remove me.

222
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:12,557
You can try to tear me
off by force if you want,

223
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:16,052
but you'll end up tearing off
your own back along the way!

224
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:23,220
Hey, you're just going
to exhaust yourself.

225
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:28,480
I wonder, will you collapse
from the trauma and fatigue?

226
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:31,073
Or will you go insane and kill yourself?

227
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:34,377
Even the most powerful
stan in the world couldn't

228
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:37,636
beat this weaklings gift for
gab and utter domination!

229
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,030
Yes!

230
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:43,420
A stan that clings to backs!

231
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:44,836
This is too bizarre!

232
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:49,240
Bizarre. So true. Have a look.

233
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,880
You know you want to.

234
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:53,960
Do it.

235
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,560
I'm happy to give you a peek.

236
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,320
He's finally lost his mind!

237
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:16,521
Now you realize a visit
to Jotaro would be futile!

238
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:18,610
Jotaro?

239
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:22,718
I never had any intention
of ever paying him a visit.

240
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:24,432
This was my destination.

241
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:27,620
I was beside myself
that I finally made it.

242
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:29,460
I can't help but laugh.

243
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:32,337
What's with all the rambling?

244
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:35,126
You finally exposed your
back to another soul!

245
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:37,780
Now I get to pass into Koichi Hirose!

246
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:40,070
Wait!

247
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:41,420
I know this street!

248
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:42,975
This is where we met!

249
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:46,720
Cheap trap, you picked a hell
of a place to turn around.

250
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:50,797
Even if you had known about this
place and resisted turning around,

251
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:54,137
you would have still had no
choice but to look Koichi's way?

252
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:56,044
thanks to your special ability.

253
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:58,920
What the hell?

254
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,182
We're walking down Rainy Street!

255
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:06,817
Looking back's a death wish!

256
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:10,597
You were right about no stand being
able to remove you from my back.

257
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:13,037
You'd just end up hurting me if you tried.

258
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:15,826
However, there is something
that can take you.

259
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:19,353
Something that latches on to
those who dare to look back.

260
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:22,088
Something that'll carry
away your very soul.

261
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,480
Let me go!

262
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:26,060
Please let me go, yes!

263
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:28,297
Where are these things gonna take me?

264
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:29,210
Answer!

265
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,820
To the other side.

266
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:34,357
I can't say for sure whether
there's a heaven or a hell,

267
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:36,675
but a simple memo should do the trick.

268
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:53,969
For a stand that does nothing but talk,
he was quite a little terror, Koichi.

269
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:56,077
If you hadn't have shown up when you did,

270
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:59,257
I'm sure I wouldn't still
be around to tell the tale.

271
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:01,297
I had no clue this is where we ended up.

272
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:04,027
I was too focused on
that freaky enemy stand.

273
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:07,690
It's Reimi.

274
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,500
Hey, Rohan.

275
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:12,580
Did you take these pictures? Yes. Why?

276
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:14,200
Check this out.

277
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:15,680
How strange.

278
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:27,000
Did you hear?

279
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:31,535
Mika got her boyfriend to buy her a
brand new pair of designer earrings.

280
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:33,597
What do you say you buy me some?

281
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:34,680
Maybe next time.

282
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:40,517
The hell you think you're doing, skis?

283
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:41,953
You can't come in here!

284
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:43,452
Get out of my apartment!

285
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,140
Hmm, a studio apartment.

286
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,820
My name is Yoshikage Kira.

287
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:01,627
Would you be so kind as
to tell me your name?

288
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:06,340
They don't look normal, do they?

289
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:08,746
Look how long they've gotten.

290
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:11,017
Do you think there's a single soul on the

291
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:13,577
planet who can keep
their nails from growing?

292
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:14,520
There isn't.

293
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:17,920
No one can stop a nail's destiny to grow.

294
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:22,857
Just as there's no one who can truly
suppress the inner passions one is born with.

295
00:15:22,940 --> 00:15:26,160
Now, I believe I asked
you to tell me your name.

296
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:28,197
What did you do to my boyfriend?

297
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:29,697
He was right here before...

298
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:32,057
Don't ever answer a
question with a question!

299
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:35,617
You did learn proper etiquette while
you were in school now, didn't you?

300
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:38,117
I'm asking you to tell
me what your name is!

301
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,030
Minako!

302
00:15:39,113 --> 00:15:40,180
My name is Minako!

303
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:43,390
Minako.

304
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:48,020
What a beautiful name your
parents bestowed upon you.

305
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:49,280
I approve.

306
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:57,037
Minako I have a little request if
you don't mind I would be thrilled if

307
00:15:57,120 --> 00:16:02,317
you could hold on to these for me and
I'd greatly appreciate it if you could

308
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:07,297
trim my robust nails with these lame
clippers you've never done this before

309
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:10,937
have you it's your lucky day now don't

310
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:15,500
cut them too short someone help me?

311
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:18,120
I'm sorry!

312
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,980
Forgive me! Forgive you?

313
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,840
Now, wait just a minute.

314
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:27,197
I'm not the least bit angry if
that's what's concerning you.

315
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,680
You intrigue me.

316
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,235
I chose you because of our connection.

317
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:36,465
I was born with a certain set of desires,
so I simply try to make the most of it.

318
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:38,213
Life's better that way.

319
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:41,897
You were begging your boyfriend
for a pair of earrings, yeah?

320
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:43,420
He left these for you.

321
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:45,079
What do you think?

322
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:52,580
You truly are a deft nail-cutter.

323
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:54,460
How I adore you.

324
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:01,300
I dare say you're even
cuter when you're silent.

325
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:04,860
So what to do now, my dear?

326
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:07,414
I'd love to take you back home with me.

327
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:10,266
But I don't think the
Kawajiris would approve.

328
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,880
Oh, how I've missed the sensation.

329
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:15,720
I feel so complete.

330
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:23,640
So that man and woman he
followed here from the station,

331
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:26,240
he completely vaporized them.

332
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:39,590
What?

333
00:17:39,673 --> 00:17:40,503
That's Hayato.

334
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:42,720
What could he be doing here?

335
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:47,109
This is in the opposite direction
from the house and school.

336
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:48,820
What's that?

337
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:55,960
Damn it, I forgot to lock the door.

338
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,120
Could Hayato have?

339
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:05,040
It couldn't be.

340
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:09,960
There's no way he's human.

341
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:12,711
Why is that demon pretending to be my dad?

342
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:32,591
This might be evidence that he's returned.

343
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,980
I'm pretty sure this is blood.

344
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:40,540
So Kira's finally made his move.

345
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,680
I'm absolutely positive.

346
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:59,167
Hayato is holding a
video camera in his hand.

347
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:03,620
It doesn't seem to be
anywhere in his room.

348
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:08,140
I've definitely noticed
Hayato acting strange lately.

349
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:10,580
What is that boy up to?

350
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:12,580
I have to find out.

351
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:15,020
I need to know for sure.

352
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:18,620
I have to calm down. Breathe, Hayato.

353
00:19:18,980 --> 00:19:21,333
Just calm down and gather your thoughts.

354
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:26,496
First, I need to deal with this tape.

355
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,340
Should I show it to someone?

356
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:31,560
It can't be Mom.

357
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:34,428
She has complete and
total faith in the guy.

358
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,504
Should I show it to the police?

359
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:41,247
Would they believe that I witnessed a
man being vaporized right in front of me?

360
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:42,857
What am I saying?

361
00:19:42,940 --> 00:19:44,352
He's not a normal human!

362
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:47,397
Could the police even
catch someone like him?

363
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:52,127
Is there anyone in the world who has what
it takes to catch a monster like him?

364
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:53,680
What do I do?

365
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:56,628
Sooner or later, he's
gonna kill Mom and me.

366
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:58,560
What am I gonna do?

367
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:05,930
Evening.

368
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:08,460
Is there any room in there left for me?

369
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:12,520
Can dear old dad join you?

370
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:15,600
Why the odd face?

371
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:17,113
We've done this before.

372
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:23,837
Oh, I was actually just
finishing up and...

373
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:24,802
Don't be silly.

374
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,360
I am your father.

375
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:28,229
We should do some bonding.

376
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:31,051
What's he planning to do?

377
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:34,180
If he finds this tape, it's all over.

378
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:39,340
Sorry to be a bother, but I'll need
to use that bucket for the bath. Huh?

379
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,780
I'd like to wash the long
day away with some water.

380
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:44,530
No!

381
00:20:44,613 --> 00:20:47,676
Since we're bonding, I'll
wash your bath for you, Dad!

382
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:48,850
Hmm?

383
00:20:48,933 --> 00:20:50,120
What a splendid idea.

384
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,200
But, please allow me to
wash your back first.

385
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:59,157
You've been in the bath for
a while, so it's only fair.

386
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,620
We can just take turns.

387
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,096
How does that sound?

388
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:04,200
Here, sit.

389
00:21:12,660 --> 00:21:13,700
What is it?

390
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:16,517
You're sweating like a guilty
little pig ripe for slaughter.

391
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:17,797
or did the heat get to you?

392
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:18,860
No, I'm fine.

393
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:20,757
Just look at the way you're shaking.

394
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:21,899
You can't be fine.

395
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:27,346
It'd be rather odd for a person to tremble
after being in the bath for too long.

396
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,057
He cut it out there!

397
00:21:29,140 --> 00:21:29,970
The tickles!

398
00:21:30,053 --> 00:21:32,137
You can't touch my back
there because I freak out!

399
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:34,279
I've only told you a million times!

400
00:21:36,780 --> 00:21:39,040
How silly of me. You're right.

401
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:42,580
You always were a ticklish one, Hayato.

402
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:45,499
I'll take care of the front myself.

403
00:21:45,620 --> 00:21:47,502
I'd be happy to lend you a hand.

404
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:52,939
By the way, I wanted to
talk to you about something.

405
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:54,210
This evening,

406
00:21:54,293 --> 00:21:58,456
I was doing some work errands in the
opposite end of town near Jozenji,

407
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:00,380
when I happened to see you.

408
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:03,620
And you were holding a video camera.

409
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:06,096
What could you have been doing there?

410
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:08,200
I've got him.

411
00:22:08,820 --> 00:22:11,780
I knew this sleuthing
shit was spying on me.

412
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:13,880
I can't believe it.

413
00:22:14,540 --> 00:22:17,477
So much for casually
assimilating into this family.

414
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:20,140
It has been one catastrophe after another.

415
00:22:20,420 --> 00:22:21,580
A year of hell.

416
00:22:22,380 --> 00:22:26,340
Killing this punk will cause a
commotion, and a bad one at that.

417
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:28,020
But he saw everything.

418
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:29,660
I have no choice.

419
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:34,260
A strand of this brat's hair
now functions as a bomb.

420
00:22:34,580 --> 00:22:37,400
All it'll take is a
small blast to his skull,

421
00:22:37,540 --> 00:22:40,775
and it'll appear he simply
slipped and bumped his head.

422
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:43,297
People slip and fall in
the bathroom all the time.

423
00:22:43,380 --> 00:22:47,740
So it's time for you to die past
so you're gonna kill me, too

424
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,280
Take a look around pops.

425
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:53,812
I'm recording everything that's happening

426
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,977
I've never trusted you. fraud!

427
00:23:00,060 --> 00:23:04,077
I've recorded all your weird shoe sizes
and signature practice accessions.

428
00:23:04,160 --> 00:23:05,417
And that's not all!

429
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:08,480
I taped that cat plant
living in the attic, too?

430
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:13,917
Only I know where all the tapes are, but
if something terrible were to happen to me,

431
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,588
I'm sure someone would
find them eventually.

432
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:18,160
Where do you get off?

433
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:20,177
You're not gonna lay a finger on me!

434
00:23:20,260 --> 00:23:21,090
We clear?

435
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,157
How dare you?

436
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:25,920
You think you could
threaten the likes of me?

437
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:28,460
And that goes double for Mom!

438
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:39,777
Break it down.

439
00:23:39,860 --> 00:23:41,460
Break out.
